<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The armoury's bills (era-arc finding 5: eras buy strength, not bodies; system crafting.billcreators). Its own
    file, per CLAUDE.md. Crafting.Armoury decides which of these a bench works and for how many citizens:
    the best ranged weapon and the best armour of each slot whose materials are in reach.

    Every era's research now makes something a defender carries: bows (Agrarian Bows), the recurve bow and the
    helmet (Bronze), the great bow and mail (Classical), crossbow, musket and plate (Medieval), revolver, rifle and
    flak vest (Industrial), assault rifle (Information). The gate is each item's own research
    (ThingDef.researchPrerequisites), repeated here as the recipe's.

    RimWorld makes bows at a crafting spot or table, guns at a machining table and armour at a smithy; this
    content has one smithy and one tailoring bench, so all weapons and metal armour are the smithy's and the hide
    coat is the tailor's. RimWorld guns also take components, which this content does not have (Buildings_Shelter.xml
    makes the same substitution): steel stands in. workAmount follows the knife's scale (RimWorld's WorkToMake x
    about 0.3, Recipes_Smithing.xml); the WorkToMake values and wood counts it scales are RECALLED, the crossbow's
    and musket's unsourced. Metal armour takes its stuff from the ingredient, as the ladder's blades do. What the
    tests pin is which bill the armoury queues and for whom, not these numbers.
  -->

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Make_Bow_Short</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Bows</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>make a short bow</label>
    <jobString>Making a short bow.</jobString>
    <workAmount>1200</workAmount>
    <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>WoodLog</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>30</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><Bow_Short>1</Bow_Short></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>Smithy</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

